                    e^{- i E(\vec k) (x-y)^0 - \vec k \cdot (\vec x - \vec y)}
                    \-
                    e^{+ i E(\vec k) (x-y)^0 + \vec k \cdot (\vec x - \vec y)}
                    \\right) d^p \vec k
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \-i (2\pi)^{-p} \int \delta( k_\mu k^\mu + m^2 ) sgn( k_0 ) e^{ - i k_\mu (x-y)^\mu } d^{p+1} k
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          %p
            (e. g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Scharf01"} Scharf 01 (1.1.13)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
              the general solution to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
              may be expressed in the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
