                      denotes the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
                      of
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo ,
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma,e)
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+differential+form"} horizontal differential form
                      on
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi J
                                %mn ∞
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Σ
                              %mo ×
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^\infty(\Sigma \times k)
          %p
            The analogue of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IntegralKernelForPoissonBracketOfFreeScalarFieldOnMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            holds true for general spacetimes:
          #FreeScalarFieldGreenFunctions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
            %p
              On a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time+orientation"} time oriented
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetime"} globally hyperbolic spacetime
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+operator"} Klein-Gordon operator
              admits unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "BaerGinouxPfaeffle07"} Bär-Ginoux-Pfäffle 07, corollary 3.4.3
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
              of the free scalar field (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianOfFreeScalarField"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peierls+bracket"} Peierls bracket
          %p
            By
            %a{:href => "Peierls+bracket#PeierlsPoissonBracket"} this prop.
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Peierls+bracket#Khavkine14"} Khavkine 14
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Collini16"} Collini 16, lemma 21
            %a{:href => "locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory#FredenhagenRejzner15"} Fredenhagen-Rejzner 15, 3.3 Example
          %h3#interacting_scalar_field Interacting scalar field
          %p
            We discuss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            of the free scalar field perturbed by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            term via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative algebraic quantum field theory
          %h4#on_minkowski_spacetime_2 On Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            We disscuss the interacting scalar field on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
            we need to determine the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-point+function"} 2-point function
            with the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo .
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_A(x.y) \coloneqq \theta((x-y)^0) \Delta(x,y)
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo .
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_R(x.y) \coloneqq \theta((y-x)^0) \Delta(x,y)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phi%5En-theory"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^n
                  \-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-scalar+field"} pseudo-scalar field
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+equation"}> wave equation
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klein-Gordon+equation"} Klein-Gordon equation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+propagator"}> causal propagator
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#references References
          %p For instance
          %ul
            %li#Scharf01
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%BCnter+Scharf"}> Günter Scharf
              , section 1.1 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Gauge+Theories+--+A+True+Ghost+Story"}> Quantum Gauge Theories – A True Ghost Story
                , Wiley 2001
          %p
            Most of the literatur on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"} perturbative AQFT
            focuses on the scalar field, for ease of exposition. See the references there.
          %p
            The standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            (made rigorous via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interacting
            scalar field is shown to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fedosov+deformation+quantization"} Fedosov deformation quantization
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            in
          %ul
            %li#Collini16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Collini"}> Giovanni Collini
              , section 2.2 of
              %em Fedosov Quantization and Perturbative Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.09626"}> arXiv:1603.09626
              )
          %p
            For references on the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
            scalar field theory in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative quantum field theory
          %p
            Discussion of scalar fields in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              J.W. van Holten,
              %em On single scalar field cosmology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.1174"}> arXiv:1301.1174
              )
          %p
            Examples in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+quantum+field+theory"} interacting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field+theory"} scalar field theory
            in
            %em any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            (in particular in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \geq 4
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Detlev+Buchholz"}> Detlev Buchholz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              %em
                A
                = succeed "-algebraic" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C*
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.06062"}> arXiv:1902.06062
              )
